responsive in this way because it doesn't suffer from context switching like us mortals do.

00:03:42.479 --> 00:03:48.639
So increasingly, we found ourselves thinking like, all right, Cloud's really good at solving

00:03:48.639 --> 00:03:53.679
this problem. I wonder what else I could point it out. What else is out there that maybe

00:03:55.279 --> 00:04:01.039
we have found to be hard and challenging that maybe it's not so challenging anymore?

00:04:01.679 --> 00:04:08.720
And so a number of months ago, I started looking at how we were responding to

00:04:09.679 --> 00:04:17.920
customer support queries. So again, as many of you probably know, Posit uses Zendesk for support.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:23.839
So you all can file tickets there, and our support team will respond to them. And if it's

00:04:25.279 --> 00:04:29.920
something that has a well-established answer, they can respond to you with that. But if it's

