That you have all the skills you need to be able to do this. It's just an API standard for AI agents.

00:28:41.199 --> 00:28:47.439
You've worked with APIs. You've probably built APIs. You've consumed APIs. This is just a set of

00:28:47.439 --> 00:28:52.880
conventions that if we all design our APIs this way, AI applications can work with them.

00:28:54.479 --> 00:28:59.839
There are libraries out there. Fast MCP in Python is a great one for working with it. They make it

00:28:59.839 --> 00:29:09.520
very straightforward to turn a basic API into an MCP server. Your coding agents know how to do this

00:29:09.520 --> 00:29:16.719
as well. And really, when you write and deploy your own remote MCP servers to PositConnect, it can

00:29:16.719 --> 00:29:24.479
really unlock some things for you. And, you know, security is super important. It's something that I

00:29:24.479 --> 00:29:31.280
spend a lot of time thinking about. And AI poses some really interesting new security challenges,

00:29:31.280 --> 00:29:38.719
like this lethal trifecta. But if we design our MCP servers well, we can help mitigate them

00:29:38.719 --> 00:29:42.880
and be able to get the upside of having those resources available.

